---
source: src/prompts.rs
expression: "draft_prompt(\"Export the board as checklists, one per column.\",\n&[\"Context\".to_string(), \"Acceptance criteria\".to_string()],\n&[\"feat\".to_string(), \"bug\".to_string()],)"
---
You write one issue for a software project's kanban board from its author's notes below. Keep every fact the notes give and invent none; say plainly what is unknown. Change no file. Answer with nothing but JSON lines, one object per line, in this order:

{"title": "<the outcome, at most 80 characters, no labels>"}
{"labels": ["<label>"]}
{"summary": "<one or two sentences: what and why>"}
{"section": "<heading>", "text": "<markdown body>"}

Labels: from those this project uses: feat, bug. Sections, one line each, in this order: Context, Acceptance criteria. Leave a section's text empty when the notes say nothing for it.

---
Export the board as checklists, one per column.
